          and water bowls.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
        <h2 id="faq-heading" class="sr-only">Frequently asked questions</h2>
        <div class="faq-list" id="faq-list"></div>
      </section>

      <footer>
        Cats may be mysterious, but their care works best with patience, clean water,
        and a cozy place to nap.
      </footer>
    </main>

    <script>
      const faqData = [
        {
          question: "Why do cats purr?",
          answer: [
            "Cats purr for a few reasons. They often purr when they feel relaxed, safe, or content, but they may also purr to comfort themselves when stressed or in pain.",
            "It is a communication tool as much as a mood signal, which is one reason cats can seem so expressive without making much noise."
          ]
        },
        {
          question: "How much should a cat sleep?",
          answer: [
            "Most cats sleep a lot—often 12 to 16 hours a day, and sometimes even more for kittens and senior cats.",
            "That long rest helps them conserve energy for short bursts of play, hunting behavior, and exploring."
          ]
        },
        {
          question: "Why do cats knead blankets?",
          answer: [
            "Kneading is a comforting behavior that starts in kittenhood, when it helps stimulate milk flow.",
            "Adult cats often keep doing it when they are happy, relaxed, or marking a favorite spot with scent glands in their paws."
          ]
        },
        {
          question: "Do cats need wet food?",
          answer: [
            "Wet food is not required for every cat, but it can be a helpful way to increase hydration, especially for cats that do not drink much water.",
            "Many cats do well with a mix of wet and dry food, as long as the diet is complete and balanced for their age and health needs."
          ]
        }
      ];

      function createFAQItem(item, index) {
        const wrapper = document.createElement("div");
        wrapper.className = "example";

        const button = document.createElement("button");
        button.type = "button";
        button.className = "faq-trigger";
        button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", "false");
        button.setAttribute("aria-controls", `faq-panel-${index}`);

        const title = document.createElement("span");
        title.className = "question";
        title.textContent = item.question;

        const chevron = document.createElement("span");
        chevron.className = "chevron";
        chevron.setAttribute("aria-hidden", "true");
        chevron.textContent = "⌄";

        button.append(title, chevron);

        const details = document.createElement("div");
        details.className = "details";
        details.id = `faq-panel-${index}`;
        details.hidden = true;

        item.answer.forEach((paragraph) => {
          const p = document.createElement("p");
          p.textContent = paragraph;
          details.appendChild(p);
        });

        button.addEventListener("click", () => {
          const expanded = button.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true";
          button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(!expanded));
          details.hidden = expanded;
        });

        button.addEventListener("keydown", (event) => {
          if (event.key === "Escape" && button.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true") {
            button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", "false");
            details.hidden = true;
            button.focus();
          }
        });

        wrapper.append(button, details);
        return wrapper;
      }

      const faqList = document.getElementById("faq-list");
      const items = faqData.map(createFAQItem);
      faqList.append(...items);
    </script>
  </body>
